# Local CLI for tests

Global `routekit` (PATH / pnpm bin) is for **config and setup only**: remotes, tokens, `status`, `config`, `accounts`, `providers`.

Every **test, eval, probe, or behavior check** must use the repo CLI, not the global binary:

```bash
node packages/cli/dist/index.js <cmd>
# or
pnpm dev:run-routekit -- <cmd>
```

Build first if `packages/cli/dist/index.js` is missing (`pnpm build` or `pnpm build:cli`).

```bash
# ❌ BAD — testing eval/gateway behavior with whatever is on PATH
routekit eval run --spec suite.json --url … --token …

# ✅ GOOD — same check against this checkout
node packages/cli/dist/index.js eval run --spec suite.json --url … --token …
```

`--remote` on the global CLI is fine for reading orbit URL/token/models. Do not use that binary to exercise product commands under test (`eval`, `policy`, gateway probes of new code).
